          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What does guidance describe about starting a statin, and which risk bands are used?",
          "answer": "The search results only partly answer your question, so I can't describe the statin risk bands from them.\n\n**From the lipid screening and statin initiation guidance:** The retrieved text includes a few fragments. It says that when screening is normal, the usual repeat interval is three years, and shorter if risk factors build up or weight increases. It also says a lower body-mass-index threshold applies to people of Asian ancestry. A section on \"diagnostic thresholds\" is mentioned, but its contents were cut off. The passage on how risk is banded and when a statin is started was not included. Part of the result was also removed by the system, so I can't fill that gap.\n\n**From the coronary artery disease secondary prevention guidance:** This covers people who already have a diagnosis of coronary artery disease. It lists high-intensity statin therapy as part of standard care. It notes that US guidance describes the statin intensity, while European guidance sets an LDL cholesterol goal instead. If the response is inadequate, other non-statin medicines are added rather than the statin being stopped.\n\nThese passages do not explain how a person without a diagnosis is placed into a risk band, or what threshold triggers starting a statin. A clinician can go through your own risk factors and the current guidance with you. Please don't change any medicine based on this summary.\n\n*Not medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.*",
